@title Quote Pricing Model Architecture
@subtitle Orchard Insurance real-time pricing
@author ML Platform
@date Reviewed 2026-10-12

## Overview

The quote pricing service prices about 450 quotes per second at peak, with a p99 latency target of 250 ms. Agents request prices from the portal; a Lambda gathers cached features and calls a SageMaker endpoint for the prediction.

## Architecture diagram

diagram pricing dir=LR title="Real-time quote pricing"
pricing: portal "Agent Portal" user
pricing: apigw "API Gateway" lb
pricing: lambda "Inference Lambda" fn focus
pricing: sm "SageMaker Endpoint" svc focus
pricing: cache "Feature Cache" cache
pricing: shadow "Shadow Endpoint" svc
pricing: bucket "Model Bucket" store
pricing: training "Training Pipeline" svc
pricing: registry "Model Registry" store
pricing: portal -> apigw : quote request
pricing: apigw -> lambda : invoke
pricing: lambda -> cache : get features
pricing: lambda -> sm : predict
pricing: lambda -> shadow : mirrored traffic
pricing: training -> registry : register model
pricing: registry -> bucket : approved artifact
pricing: bucket --> sm : load model
pricing: group infvpc "Inference VPC" lambda, sm, cache, shadow
pricing: group prod "Prod account" apigw, bucket, infvpc
pricing: group ml "ML account" training, registry

## Capacity

table = Component,Size,Scaling; SageMaker Endpoint,ml.c6i.2xlarge,4 to 12 instances on invocations per instance; Inference Lambda,1024 MB,200 reserved concurrency; Feature Cache,cache.r7g.large,2 replicas; Shadow Endpoint,ml.c6i.xlarge,2 instances

## Deployment

1. Register the model.
2. Approve it in Model Registry.
3. Blue/green deploy, shifting 10% of traffic every 5 minutes.
4. Roll back automatically if p99 exceeds 250 ms.

!! The Feature Cache is not a source of truth. A cache miss falls back to the policy database and adds about 90 ms.
